---
/**
 * Shown when a site has no Site Assets library (SKYE stores its data there
 * and can't create the library itself). Explains it, links to SharePoint's
 * "add a page" flow (which provisions Site Assets), and offers "Check
 * again". wireCreateSiteAssetsStep() (src/lib/routing/siteSwitcher.ts)
 * fills the site name + link, wires the buttons, and returns
 * { setStatus, setBusy } that entry-switcher.ts's auto-poll drives.
 */
---

<section class="skye-site-switcher skye-create-assets" data-state id="step-create-assets" hidden>
  <h2>One step in SharePoint first</h2>
  <p>
    <span data-slot="site-name"></span> doesn't have a Site Assets library
    yet — that's where SKYE keeps its data, and SKYE can't create it for
    you. The quickest way: open a new page in SharePoint and save it (even
    as a draft) — that creates Site Assets automatically. Then come back
    and check again.
  </p>
  <a class="skye-create-assets__link" data-el="create-link" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
    Add a page in SharePoint ↗
  </a>
  <menu class="skye-create-assets__row">
    <li><button class="skye-create-assets__cancel" data-el="cancel" type="button">Cancel</button></li>
    <li><button class="skye-create-assets__retry" data-el="retry" type="button">Check again</button></li>
  </menu>
  <output class="skye-create-assets__status" data-el="status"></output>
</section>
